.TH PURR 1 "September 2026" "purr 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
purr \- Universal Application Discovery and Priority Installer for Arch Linux & KDE Plasma
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B purr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR...]
.br
.B purr
\fBupgrade\fR|\fBupdate\fR|\fBup\fR
.br
.B purr
\fBself-update\fR
.br
.B purr
\fBrepair\fR \fIAPP_NAME\fR [\fI--force\fR]
.br
.B purr
\fBrecipe\fR [\fIlist\fR|\fIinfo\fR|\fIapply\fR|\fIsync\fR|\fIdoctor\fR|\fIprune\fR|\fIteardown\fR] [\fIRECIPE_ID\fR]
.br
.B purr
\fBapk\fR [\fIrepair\fR|\fIinstall\fR|\fIlaunch\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIcertify\fR|\fIsession\fR|\fIpaste\fR] [\fIARG\fR]
.br
.B purr
\fBtray\fR [\fI--daemon\fR] [\fI-i INTERVAL\fR] [\fI--initial-delay SECONDS\fR]
.br
.B purr
\fBintegrate\fR [\fIINTEGRATION_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpurr\fR (Project Tuki) is an intelligent, multi-source universal package discovery engine, priority installer, and modular ecosystem recipe framework engineered for Arch Linux and KDE Plasma. It abstracts disparate packaging ecosystems (Pacman official repos, Arch Linux CN, Arch User Repository (AUR), Flatpak/Flathub, AppImage, and reproducible Subsystem Recipes) into a unified, heuristic-driven 1-click experience.
.PP
Purr understands human queries with spaces and informal names, resolves canonical slugs and brand aliases, weighs community trust and AUR popularity, suppresses auxiliary noise (such as extensions, plugins, and drivers), and executes clean, non-interactive installations.
.PP
Dedicated to \fBTuki\fR (2019\(en2024), "The Calm Before and After All Storms".
.SH PACKAGING HIERARCHY
When resolving queries, \fBpurr\fR strictly enforces the following hierarchy:
.IP [1] 4
\fBSystem Repositories\fR (\fIcore\fR, \fIextra\fR, \fImultilib\fR, \fIendeavouros\fR, \fIarchlinuxcn\fR) via \fBpacman\fR
.IP [2] 4
\fBArch User Repository (AUR)\fR via \fByay\fR
.IP [3] 4
\fBFlatpak\fR sandboxed containers via \fBflathub\fR
.IP [4] 4
\fBAppImage\fR portable bundles via \fBgearlever\fR / standalone
.IP [5] 4
\fBGit\fR direct upstream source repositories
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B [query...]
Searches all package backends concurrently, scores matching applications using heuristic ranking, and prompts for confirmation before non-interactive installation.
.TP
.B upgrade, update, up \fR[\fI--auto-sync\fR]\fP
Performs an automated universal system upgrade across official Pacman repositories, the AUR, Flatpaks, and deployed subsystem recipes. Automatically checks and removes stale database locks (\fI/var/lib/pacman/db.lck\fR), refreshes out-of-date system keyrings on signature errors, automatically confirms package replacements (\fI--ask 4\fR), overwrites unowned conflicting files (\fI--overwrite "*"\fR), auto-prunes unsupported and EOL Flatpak runtimes, and non-destructively converges deployed subsystem recipes (updating companion APKs, framework patches, and KWin rules with zero data loss). If \fB--auto-sync\fR or \fB--sync-subsystems\fR is specified, or if \fIsubsystem_auto_sync\fR is enabled in configuration, deployed recipes are converged automatically without prompt. Upon completion, immediately triggers an IPC refresh to update the background system tray icon.
.TP
.B self-update
Checks for and installs host Purr updates. Pulls latest release tags and updates binaries from git checkout or upgrades the package via yay.
.TP
.B repair \fIAPP_NAME\fR [\fI--force\fR]
Headlessly diagnoses, repairs, and enforces binary architecture compatibility for Android subsystem applications (e.g. recovering Facebook Messenger from 64-bit translation crash loops by locking it to a 32-bit ARM build and immunizing it against Google Play Store auto-updates via PurrBridgeHelper).
.TP
.B recipe [\fIlist\fR|\fIinfo\fR|\fIapply\fR|\fIsync\fR|\fIdoctor\fR|\fIprune\fR|\fIteardown\fR] [\fIRECIPE_ID\fR]
Manages declarative, reproducible ecosystem recipes (such as \fBwaydroid-native\fR for turnkey Android multi-window, ARM translation, and KDE Plasma 6 desktop integration). The \fBsync\fR subcommand non-destructively aligns deployed container state with current assets without wiping user data.
.TP
.B apk [\fIrepair\fR|\fIinstall\fR|\fIlaunch\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIcertify\fR|\fIsession\fR|\fIpaste\fR] [\fIARG\fR]
Direct Android subsystem and application manager. Supports headless app repair, direct APK installation, app launching, Google Play Protect device ID registration helper, host-to-Android clipboard injection into active input fields, and container session management.
.TP
.B tray [\fI--daemon\fR] [\fI-i MINUTES\fR] [\fI--initial-delay SECONDS\fR]
Launches the Purr System Tray Indicator and background update monitor.
.TP
.B integrate [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Configures native KDE Plasma 6 desktop integrations (Kickoff favorites, Task Manager pinning, Autostart).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays the built-in help message and exits.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Displays version information and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Searches and resolves the best matching package without performing actual installation.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-loop
Exits immediately after installing a single application instead of staying in the interactive search session loop.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/purr/config.json
User preferences for update check intervals and initial startup delay.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/purr/refresh_trigger
IPC trigger file used to signal immediate tray indicator badge updates.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/purr/apks/
Cached Android application packages for instant offline recovery (e.g. com.facebook.orca-32bit.apk).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/purr
Default executable binary location.
